# VeilBridge (#47): the LAN may send traffic into the panel's tunnel. The
# tunnel's interface is in no fw4 zone, and fw4 rejects forwarding to an
# interface outside its zones; a rule in another nftables table cannot undo
# that (measured), so it lives here, in fw4's own chain, through fw4's include
# directory. At the end of the chain: the owner's own rules for traffic from
# the LAN come first and still apply to traffic bound for the tunnel. Guests
# are not let in: this is the lan zone's chain only.
oifname "awg0" counter accept comment "VeilBridge: LAN to the tunnel"
